Interface decisions that spec.md did not fix are pinned in each test header:
- real-work.ts: `--input <file> --out <folder>`. It writes `real-work.json`
  with schema `model-guide-real-work/1`. The exit-2 line is
  `input-check: <check>` on stdout. The checks are manifest, sha256, size,
  schema, and run-sum, in that order.
- The output rate is rounded to 4 decimals. The blocking rate is rounded to
  3 decimals. The trend uses the last 4 ISO weeks present in `weekly`.
- preview.sh: `--export <file>`, optional `--preview <folder>`, default
  `<repo>/.tmp/model-guide-preview`. It resolves the repo root three levels
  above the script. It writes `real-work.json`, `real-work.html`, and
  `preview-base.json`. It writes no file under `docs/`.
- preview-base.json: `{schema:"model-guide-preview-base/1",docs:{<path>:<sha>}}`.
- publish.ts: `--preview <folder>`, run from `<repo>/harness`. The approval
  record is `<repo>/measure/tracks/model_guide/publish-approval.md`. Its
  format is `approved_by:`, `date:`, `files:`, then `<sha256>  <path>` lines.
  The checks run approval, approved sha, drift, copy. The lines are
  `publish: no approval record`, `publish: sha256 <path>`, and
  `publish: drift <path>`.
- Added case: `preview-gate.test.ts` case 7 is a success case for the publish
  copy. Plan task 1.3 lists only refusals. Without case 7, a tool that always
  exits 2 would pass.

